n hold of Webster's open seat. A lone Democratic-sponsored poll showing a tie is outweighed by fundamentals and prediction markets pricing the Democrat near 12%.", "watch": "A fresh independent poll showing the race near even, or a late Democratic outside-spending surge, would move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 58 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Open seat: Daniel Webster (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Republicans are favored to hold this open Central Florida seat after Daniel Webster's retirement. Joe Strada survived a razor-thin GOP primary recount over Carey Baker and enters the general with a massive money edge, having raised $5.2 million to Democrat James Pericola's $120,000. The district leans Republican by seven points on recent partisan performance.\n\nMost raters call the race Likely R, with several rating it Solid or Safe R, and prediction markets give the Democrat roughly a one-in-eight chance. The only public poll, a Democratic-sponsored survey from late July, showed a 42-42 tie, but its sponsorship and age limit its weight. A Libertarian candidate is also on the ballot. The expectation is a Republican win in the high single digits to low teens, with meaningful uncertainty given the thin polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1071, "margin": -7.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1312, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1199, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0703, "margin": -10.0}]}